From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Draven <dravengarden@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:04:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bound JSONL frames and stop the native process on a lost
 frame

The reader searches incoming bytes once, preserves split UTF-8
sequences and assembles each completed frame once, up to 256 MiB.
A malformed, oversized or incomplete frame is fatal instead of being
skipped: it may be a lost response, whose request (including resume)
would otherwise wait forever. The connection stops the native process,
and its exit disposes the connection and rejects pending requests.

Cowboy-Delta: jsonl-frame-reader
Upstream: not-proposed
Drop-When: upstream treats malformed or oversized app-server frames as fatal with bounded memory and redacted diagnostics
Tests: src/__tests__/CowboyStdUtils.test.ts src/__tests__/CodexJsonRpcConnection.test.ts src/__tests__/StdUtils.test.ts

